<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tax hits S.Africa Sanlam's yr earnings.</title>
<headline>Tax hits S.Africa Sanlam's yr earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings for</p>
<p>     capital portfolio after-tax	 1,614 vs 2,138</p>
<p>Earnings for</p>
<p>     capital portfolio pre-tax	   1,913 vs 2,242</p>
<p>    Tax					    299 vs   104</p>
<p>    Total assets			   132,877 vs 124,987</p>
<p>    Capital				    9,304 vs   7,690</p>
<p>    Income				    28,061 vs  24,469</p>
<p>    Premium income			  18,618 vs  16,654</p>
<p>    Investment income			8,263 vs   6,899</p>
<p>    Changes in value of assets	   3,856 vs  10,246</p>
<p>    Expenditure				2,977 vs   2,767</p>
<p>Full name: Sanlam</p>
<p>NOTE - Mutually-owned life assurer Sanlam said its internal restructuring was progressing well with the aim of making the company a world class financial services group</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
